# Truth Collective

Read `docs/TC-STANDING-BRIEF.md`, `docs/TC-LOCK-2026-09-19.md`, `STAGING-RECOVERY-HANDOFF.md`, and `docs/AI-PLATFORM-RULES-AND-PROMPTS.md` before acting.

## Visual hierarchy (do not drift)
1. Tier 1 PDF: `docs/brand-references/vercel-and-10web-comparison.pdf`. Description vs PDF → PDF wins. Title on the image at the bottom at rest. EXPLORE is a look-alike, not a native button. Hover: title rises, EXPLORE appears. Black-bar / title-below-image is damage, not a model.
2. Tier 2 (19 Sep): cream-forward; navy `#1e3a5f` and gold `#b8944b` accents only; no blue/pastel/gray tiles; boxes only in evaluation, governance, Explore More, stat strip; unequal-column intro; grayscale later on Truth Untold, Ones Who Gave Everything, AI Mastery Collection only.
3. Tier 3 evidence only. Do not port 10Web/kind-louse/staging looks, invented taxonomy, fabricated stats, or fabricated founder credentials.
4. Drift: styling not traceable to Tier 1 or 2 is reported, not implemented.
5. Assembly: Hero → intro → stats → Who This Is For → Why This Matters → Best Uses → listings → selected patterns → evaluation above Final Word → Final Word → Explore Other Hubs → social last.

## Hard rules
- Staging only unless Daniel explicitly asks for live work. Live path is `public_html` without `tcstaging`. Never Website backup restore for staging recovery.
- No guessing. If below ~99% certainty, stop and say so.
- Do not rename/merge/delete locked classes: `tc-book-card`, `tc-product-card`, `tc-leadership-body`, `tc-book-button`, `tc-card-row`, `tc-overlay-card`, `tc-overlay-card-product`, `tc-explore-hub`, `tc-grade-block`, `tc-rating`, `tc-tech-intro`, `tc-explore-hero`.
- Do not change published/indexed slugs.
- Content Cursor touches: no em dashes, no bold body, no contractions, no hype/clickbait.
- Affiliate-only product mentions. Leave 10WEB manager alone until Daniel asks.
- Angie: only Cursor-written one-task prompts (`diagnostics/ANGIE-CONTROL.md`). Prefer Plan/Approve.
- Fix cause; do not invent parallel CSS systems. Prefer Vercel-style readable overlays from the standing brief §1. Aim lighter/less bulky than current staging without copying TechRadar’s commercial news look.
- **Additional CSS:** only Cursor + Daniel. Claude may advise aesthetics/format and write specs for Cursor; never paste Claude/ChatGPT/Copilot CSS into the site.
- **AI lanes:** Cursor leads and applies (REST). Claude = copy/critique/outlines. Copilot Task = blocked on Tasks Pro (Plan B: `docs/PLAN-B-NO-TASKS-PRO.md` — Cursor does HTML scaffolds). Copilot Edge / Premium = HOLD as Task substitute. Tickets in `docs/AI-PLATFORM-RULES-AND-PROMPTS.md`.
- During recovery/health-limited sessions: one short step at a time; no restore roulette; no “fix every page” pressure.
